  partName: Sensor (2)
  description: The Sensor (2) is a tiny, elongated device situated at the middle-center-front
    of the engine, tasked with monitoring critical parameters such as temperature,
    pressure, or flow rates. Made of Material.004, this sensor provides accurate
    and reliable data, enabling the engine control unit to make informed decisions.
    Notably, the sensor's elongated shape allows it to be mounted in tight spaces,
    providing easy access to vital engine components.
